The current validation mechanism in the _validateArtCreationSignature function is insufficient because it only verifies the authenticity of the signature and the expiration time, without performing comprehensive checks on the actual content of the signedData_. This means that while the data may be signed by a trusted entity, the system fails to ensure that the data itself is not malicious or manipulated. As a result, an attacker can craft harmful data that, despite being correctly signed, bypasses these superficial checks and leads to unauthorized or fraudulent art creation within the contract, ultimately compromising the integrity and security of the system.

